e saying  in the long run right now we we are in  this  so volatile transitionary period uh  which is uh uh linked to a lot of  insecurity there are so many critical  uncertainties right so some countries  like australia for instance  did take a site uh this is what  australia did last year by uh entering a  security and defense pact and i argued  that in the long run a lot of regional  players in the pacific will be faced  with the same dilemma of either or  choices uh some countries like  india are going to probably uh  seek once again a very unique position  in this  rapidly shifting global orders so that  does not necessarily mean only uh siding  with the west but i suppose that india  will try to navigate carefully between  these two  emerging geopolitical blocs yeah william  just briefly where does that leave the  united states i only ask because the  special representative of the united  states is going to be part of a meeting  with china russia and pakistan today  ostensibly on afghanistan but i'm  certain that ukraine will also figure  prominently here won't it  exactly this troika format uh has been  uh  working uh so that means this one of the  opportunities for the american and the  russian counterparts but uh of course  the chinese one will be also present to  meet and discuss the relevant uh  issues of uh the international relations  and ukraine will certainly be on the  agenda even though the detroit the  detroit discusses actually afghanistan  let me also remind you that there's been  a severe famine emerging in afghanistan  so there is also a humanitarian crisis  and because of the  severe second order effects now emerging  out of russia's war on ukraine that  means uh specifically wet exports to uh  the middle east and to uh north african  countries but also asian countries and  one of these uh examples is afghanistan  there'll be there will be certainly also  a discussion on how to tackle the  humanitarian crisis and when it comes to  ukraine i do